From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 09:06:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 107/185] segacd: a trace per init step, so a boot that stops
 says where

A Mode 1 boot reached trace E005 -- the top of biosmain -- and
stopped, which locates the fault only to 'somewhere in the whole of
bios_init'. One word store per init call on a path that runs once
turns that into a number: E11F, about to call blkdev_init. Four more
inside blkdev_hdv_init narrow it to E203, about to call
disk_init_all.

So it is the disk probe, and it hangs with a disc in the tray as
readily as without one -- which kills the empty-tray theory the last
build was shipped to test.
---
 bios/bios.c   | 86 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----------------------
 bios/blkdev.c | 11 +++++++
 2 files changed, 59 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

